        "rust/sp1-comparison/tests/installed_assembly_export.rs"
      ],
      "limit": "Six installed calls: HALT, ENTER_UNCONSTRAINED, COMMIT, COMMIT_DEFERRED_PROOFS, HINT_LEN, HINT_READ. Full-word canonical codes restrict executor dispatch. WRITE and VERIFY_SP1_PROOF installation remains #12. The code guard is compared with SP1 enum values and Lean rows. The syscall instruction and installed host-call wrapper compare released supervisor rows, public bindings, shared ledgers and WRITE's register read. A regression preserves unresolved inactive-commit/empty-bitmap public-addressing drift; arbitrary-row public equivalence is not established. Closed native write-permission tests cover ROM exclusion, fixed intervals and complete ledgers; they do not implement SP1 runtime mprotect. Closed native hint-source tests authenticate literal bytes, node identities, final padding and counted ledgers. All installed host components export in the complete branch assembly, whose call tables remain empty. HALT, constrained-replay ENTER, all sixteen commitment handlers and both bank terminals compare generated rows/ledgers and released executor effects. Native per-call receipts preserve mutable bank history; a released-shard regression shows that earlier differing writes fail SP1 public-digest AIR despite the same final bank. Empty/nonempty HINT_LEN and HINT_READ handlers compare complete rows/ledgers, queue transitions and padded-write endpoints with released execution, including empty hints and limb carries. Full physical Memory coverage and complete active-host generation remain open."
    },
